<title>USA: Shell to shut Ala. gas plant next week.</title>
<headline>Shell to shut Ala. gas plant next week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Midstream Enterprises' Yellow Hammer natural gas plant in Coden, Ala., which is west of Mobile, will shut down on Wednesday, October 23, for scheduled maintenance, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Gas deliveries will return to normal by October 31, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The company could not comment on what volumes would be affected by the outage, but traders estimated that 400 million cubic feet per day of gas would be cut.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
